{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The rider cancelled 120 seconds after the driver was assigned, and the trip record shows the driver had not arrived: arrived_at is null, there is no 'arrived' event, and the only events are driver_assigned, driver_en_route and trip_cancelled. Under POL-NS-10(a) a rider's cancellation within platform_policy.grace_after_match_sec of accepted_at is not chargeable whatever the driver's position, and the record carries grace_after_match_sec of 180 seconds. The cancellation at 15:09:39 is 120 seconds after accepted_at at 15:07:39, inside the grace, so the $4.50 cancellation fee is not chargeable and must be refunded in full.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02737", "EV-FARE-02737"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-10"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.accepted_at and trip_record.cancelled_at against platform_policy.grace_after_match_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver never arrived at the pickup point. The GPS trace's derived arrival block shows driver_fix_count of 18 but qualifying_fix_count of 0 and longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec of 0.0, and the driver's minimum distance from the pickup pin across the whole trace is 6833.3 m. Under POL-NS-02 the driver is deemed to have arrived only where the trace contains at least 3 consecutive fixes within the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius, and here there are none, so POL-NS-01 limb (b) fails and the rider is entitled to a full refund of the cancellation fee.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02737", "EV-TRIP-02737"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-02", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count and derived.driver_track.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Even setting the grace period aside, the effective in-geofence dwell is zero seconds against a required minimum of 180 seconds for this STANDARD zone class, a shortfall of 180 seconds. Under POL-NS-06 the cancellation fee is not chargeable and is refunded in full where the effective dwell is shorter than the free waiting period in force, whether or not the rider was present. The trace shows no in-geofence interval at all, so the shortfall is total.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02737", "EV-TRIP-02737"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.shortfall_sec and derived.arrival.thresholds.minimum_dwell_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's own track shows him travelling at 57.1 to 62.6 km/h throughout the trace, far above the 15 km/h motion threshold, and his closest approach to the pin was 6833.3 m, far beyond the 300 m mark. Under POL-NS-05 the arrival marker is false and does not start the waiting clock; here there is no arrival marker at all and no qualifying in-geofence fix anywhere in the trip, so the fee is refunded in full and no driver compensation is payable.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02737", "EV-TRIP-02737"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.distinct_speeds_kph and derived.driver_track.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's own device was stationary at the pickup point: the rider track shows a single fix at 0.0 km/h with a distance of 8.8 m from the pin, well inside the 100 m STANDARD rider presence radius. The rider was where the booking said she would be, and the driver was 6.8 km away. This corroborates that the failure to complete the pickup was not the rider's doing.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02737"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.min_distance_m and derived.arrival.thresholds.rider_presence_radius_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The fare breakdown confirms the $4.50 cancellation fee was charged and remains charged, with payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.0. The rider's claim is that she was charged despite cancelling two minutes after booking, and the ledger shows exactly that charge standing. Under POL-GEN-03 a FULL_REFUND returns the whole contested amount to the filing party, and the contested amount is the $4.50 cancellation fee.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02737"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.cancellation_fee and fare_breakdown.payment_status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The traffic advisory artifact is MISSING with weight 0.0, so no advisory covers this pickup road in this window. Under POL-NS-06 limb (i) a traffic advisory is required to be present and populated before separate in-geofence intervals may be summed, and a MISSING advisory makes that limb unavailable. The absence is citable and it means the driver cannot rely on any kerb restriction or enforcement operation to excuse the total absence of in-geofence dwell.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02737-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "relies_on": "admissibility.status of EV-ADVIS-02737-01",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's profile shows no_show_terminations_30d of 0 and completed_trips_30d of 113, so the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip and there is no basis to withhold compensation on that ground. But compensation under POL-NS-07 is only payable where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, and here it is not: the driver never arrived and never waited. No driver compensation is owed on this record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02737", "EV-TRIP-02737"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d and driver_profile.completed_trips_30d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

