    "explanation": "Both sides agree, and the record confirms, that this $4.50 cancellation fee should not stand.\n\nTHE DECISIVE RULE — GRACE AFTER MATCH. POL-NS-10(a): a rider's cancellation within platform_policy.grace_after_match_sec of the accepted_at timestamp is not chargeable, whatever the driver's position. The trip record (EV-TRIP-02737) shows accepted_at 2026-09-15T15:07:39 (+08:00) and cancelled_at 2026-09-15T15:09:39 — 120 seconds. The record's own platform_policy sets grace_after_match_sec at 180 seconds, so the cancellation fell inside the grace. POL-NS-10(c) then requires the fee charged on that cancellation to be refunded in full with no driver compensation. The fare breakdown (EV-FARE-02737) shows the $4.50 cancellation fee was charged and remains charged (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00); that $4.50 is what is returned. This alone decides the case, and it does not depend on the driver's position.\n\nTHE INDEPENDENT GROUNDS, WHICH I ACCEPT. The driver never arrived, so POL-NS-01 is not satisfied either. The trip record carries no 'arrived' event and arrived_at is null, so limbs (a) and (b) fail; the reason code is RIDER_CANCELLED, not one of the no-show codes limb (d) recognises (RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE, EXCESSIVE_WAIT). The GPS trace (EV-GPS-02737) places the driver 6,833 m from the pin at closest approach across 18 fixes and never inside any arrival radius, so POL-NS-02 finds no qualifying in-radius fix; his reported speeds of 57.1–62.6 km/h are all above the 15 km/h motion threshold of POL-NS-05; and the effective in-geofence dwell is 0 seconds against the 180-second free waiting period, a 180-second shortfall under POL-NS-06. The rider's own device recorded a fix 8.8 m from the pin, inside the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius. Both advocates' claims on these points are accepted and point to the same refund.\n\nNO DRIVER COMPENSATION. POL-NS-07 fixes a payout only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full or POL-NS-10(g) applies; neither does, so driver_compensation_sgd is null. The anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d 0 against 113 completed trips), and the driver's other profile fields are context only under POL-GEN-01.\n\nEVIDENCE AND CONFIDENCE. The trip record, GPS trace, chat log and fare breakdown are all COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0 with no issue codes; the trace has 100% coverage, a 10 s cadence, no gaps and max_gap_sec 0.0, so nothing in POL-NS-08 limbs (a) to (d) is engaged and no cap below 1.0 applies. The empty chat log reconciles with the trip record's chat_message_count of 0 and is no defect; POL-NS-04's exoneration route simply does not operate because limb (a) needs a locating message that was never sent, and POL-NS-11 confirms an untestable rider-presence issue does not impair the driver's track. I do not rely on the missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-02737-01, weight 0.0); the claims citing it are in the discarded list for non-disclosure, and it carries nothing here.\n\nNO ESCALATION AND NO REFERRALS. No POL-NS-09 trigger fires: confidence is above the 0.70 floor, no admissible artifacts contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence, disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0 on both sides, no_show_disputes_30d is 0, the anti-farming check does not trip, and the deciding facts are carried by unimpaired artifacts. No referral is produced: no 'arrived' marker was ever pressed, so POL-NS-05(ii) has no false-arrival event to record, no driver mis-selection of a no-show reason code occurred, and no other clause directs an instruction to a reviewer. The $4.50 refund is below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold of $8.00, so it executes automatically on issue."
